{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "ada-audit-scripts",
          "version": "4.2.1",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/eedgarivann/ada-audit-scripts",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "form-label",
              "name": "FormFieldsWithoutAVisibleProgrammaticLabel",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Form fields without a visible, programmatic label"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Form fields without a visible, programmatic label. Screen-reader users hear only \"edit text\"; voice-control users cannot say the field name; everyone loses the hint once a placeholder disappears."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/tutorials/forms/labels/",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give every input, select and textarea a visible <label for=\"id\"> (placeholder text is not a label). If the design hides the label, keep it in the DOM with a visually-hidden class, never display:none. Group related controls (radio sets, date parts) in <fieldset> with a <legend>. Verify: Click the label text: focus must move into the field. In DevTools > Accessibility the field's Name equals the visible label.",
                "markdown": "1. Give every input, select and textarea a visible <label for=\"id\"> (placeholder text is not a label).\n2. If the design hides the label, keep it in the DOM with a visually-hidden class, never display:none.\n3. Group related controls (radio sets, date parts) in <fieldset> with a <legend>.\n\n**Verify:** Click the label text: focus must move into the field. In DevTools > Accessibility the field's Name equals the visible label."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG1.3.1",
                  "WCAG3.3.2",
                  "WCAG4.1.2",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "1.3.1",
                  "3.3.2",
                  "4.1.2"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "alt-missing",
              "name": "ImagesMissingAUsefulTextAlternative",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Images missing a useful text alternative"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Images missing a useful text alternative. Blind users hear a file name or nothing at all, and miss product details, prices or link destinations."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://dequeuniversity.com/rules/axe/4.14/image-alt",
              "help": {
                "text": "Informative image: alt describes what it conveys (\"Red trail lantern, 300 lumens\"). Decorative image: alt=\"\" (empty), never missing. Linked image: alt names the destination (\"Trail lantern details\"). Images of text: use real text, or put all the text in the alt. Verify: Open the images review sheet (inventory *_images.html) and compare each alt to the picture; screen reader reads a meaningful phrase.",
                "markdown": "1. Informative image: alt describes what it conveys (\"Red trail lantern, 300 lumens\").\n2. Decorative image: alt=\"\" (empty), never missing.\n3. Linked image: alt names the destination (\"Trail lantern details\").\n4. Images of text: use real text, or put all the text in the alt.\n\n**Verify:** Open the images review sheet (inventory *_images.html) and compare each alt to the picture; screen reader reads a meaningful phrase."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG1.1.1",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "1.1.1"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "change-on-input",
              "name": "PageChangesOnFocusOrInputWithoutWarning",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Page changes on focus or input without warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Page changes on focus or input without warning. Keyboard and screen-reader users are sent to a new page while just moving through a list or typing."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/on-input.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "Do not navigate on select change or on focus; add a \"Go\"/\"Apply\" button. If a change must happen, explain it before the control. Verify: Arrow through each select and Tab across fields: nothing navigates or opens until you press the button.",
                "markdown": "1. Do not navigate on select change or on focus; add a \"Go\"/\"Apply\" button.\n2. If a change must happen, explain it before the control.\n\n**Verify:** Arrow through each select and Tab across fields: nothing navigates or opens until you press the button."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG3.2.2",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "3.2.2"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "unnamed-control",
              "name": "ButtonsLinksOrIconsWithNoAccessibleName",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Buttons, links or icons with no accessible name"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Buttons, links or icons with no accessible name. Screen-reader and voice-control users hear \"button\" or \"link\" and must guess what it does."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://dequeuniversity.com/rules/axe/4.14/button-name",
              "help": {
                "text": "Give icon-only controls a name: visible text, aria-label, or visually-hidden text. Make the accessible name start with the visible label (2.5.3 Label in Name). For SVG icons inside a named control, add aria-hidden=\"true\" to the SVG. Verify: DevTools > Accessibility: each control has a Name; voice control \"click Cart\" works.",
                "markdown": "1. Give icon-only controls a name: visible text, aria-label, or visually-hidden text.\n2. Make the accessible name start with the visible label (2.5.3 Label in Name).\n3. For SVG icons inside a named control, add aria-hidden=\"true\" to the SVG.\n\n**Verify:** DevTools > Accessibility: each control has a Name; voice control \"click Cart\" works."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG4.1.2",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "4.1.2"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "contrast:1.4.3:failure",
              "name": "TextContrastTooLow",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Text contrast too low"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Text contrast too low. Low-vision users, older users and anyone on a phone in sunlight cannot read the text."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://dequeuniversity.com/rules/axe/4.14/color-contrast",
              "help": {
                "text": "Raise text contrast to at least 4.5:1 (3:1 for 24px+ or 18.66px+ bold text). Fix the design token (brand colour) once rather than per element. Check hover, focus and disabled-looking states too. Verify: Measure with a contrast checker on the rendered pixels (not just CSS): 4.5:1 or better; re-run axe color-contrast.",
                "markdown": "1. Raise text contrast to at least 4.5:1 (3:1 for 24px+ or 18.66px+ bold text).\n2. Fix the design token (brand colour) once rather than per element.\n3. Check hover, focus and disabled-looking states too.\n\n**Verify:** Measure with a contrast checker on the rendered pixels (not just CSS): 4.5:1 or better; re-run axe color-contrast."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG1.4.3",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "1.4.3"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "page-language",
              "name": "PageLanguageNotDeclared",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Page language not declared"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Page language not declared. Screen readers read the text with the wrong voice and pronunciation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://dequeuniversity.com/rules/axe/4.14/html-has-lang",
              "help": {
                "text": "Set <html lang=\"en\"> (or the page language); mark foreign-language passages with lang on the element. Verify: View source: <html lang> matches the content language.",
                "markdown": "1. Set <html lang=\"en\"> (or the page language); mark foreign-language passages with lang on the element.\n\n**Verify:** View source: <html lang> matches the content language."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG3.1.1",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "3.1.1"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "bypass-none",
              "name": "NoWayToSkipRepeatedBlocks",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No way to skip repeated blocks"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "No working way to skip repeated navigation. Keyboard and switch users must press Tab through every menu link on every page before reaching the content."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/bypass-blocks.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "Make the first focusable element a \"Skip to main content\" link. Point it at the main content: <main id=\"main\" tabindex=\"-1\">. Keep it visible when focused (do not hide it with display:none). Verify: Load the page, press Tab once: the skip link appears; press Enter, then Tab: focus lands on the first item inside the main content.",
                "markdown": "1. Make the first focusable element a \"Skip to main content\" link.\n2. Point it at the main content: <main id=\"main\" tabindex=\"-1\">.\n3. Keep it visible when focused (do not hide it with display:none).\n\n**Verify:** Load the page, press Tab once: the skip link appears; press Enter, then Tab: focus lands on the first item inside the main content."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG2.4.1",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "2.4.1"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "focus-visible:2.4.7:failure",
              "name": "NoVisibleFocusIndicator",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No visible focus indicator"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Keyboard focus is invisible. Sighted keyboard users (motor disabilities, power users, low vision) cannot see where they are on the page."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/focus-visible.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "Remove outline:none / outline:0 rules that have no replacement. Add a clear :focus-visible style (2px+ outline with 3:1 contrast against the background). Verify: Tab through the page: every focused item shows a visible ring.",
                "markdown": "1. Remove outline:none / outline:0 rules that have no replacement.\n2. Add a clear :focus-visible style (2px+ outline with 3:1 contrast against the background).\n\n**Verify:** Tab through the page: every focused item shows a visible ring."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG2.4.7",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "2.4.7"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-headings",
              "name": "PageRegionsNotMarkedUpNoMainHeadingsMissing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Page regions not marked up (no <main>, headings missing)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Page regions not marked up (no <main>, headings missing). Screen-reader users navigate by landmarks and headings; without them they must listen to the whole page."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/info-and-relationships.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "Wrap the primary content in one <main>; use <header>, <nav aria-label>, <footer>. Give each page one <h1> and use real <h2>/<h3> headings for sections (not bold text). Verify: Screen reader landmarks list (NVDA D / VoiceOver rotor) shows main and navigation; headings list reads as an outline of the page.",
                "markdown": "1. Wrap the primary content in one <main>; use <header>, <nav aria-label>, <footer>.\n2. Give each page one <h1> and use real <h2>/<h3> headings for sections (not bold text).\n\n**Verify:** Screen reader landmarks list (NVDA D / VoiceOver rotor) shows main and navigation; headings list reads as an outline of the page."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG1.3.1",
                  "WCAG2.4.1",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "1.3.1",
                  "2.4.1"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "autocomplete:1.3.5:failure",
              "name": "PersonalDataFieldMissingAutocomplete",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Personal-data field missing autocomplete"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Personal-data fields missing autocomplete. People with memory, dexterity or cognitive disabilities must retype details that the browser could fill; slow, error-prone on mobile."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/#input-purposes",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add the matching HTML autocomplete token to each field that collects the user's own data (name, email, tel, street-address, postal-code, cc-number, one-time-code...). Do not set autocomplete=\"off\" on those fields. Verify: Open the form in Chrome or Safari with a saved address/profile: each field offers autofill with the right value.",
                "markdown": "1. Add the matching HTML autocomplete token to each field that collects the user's own data (name, email, tel, street-address, postal-code, cc-number, one-time-code...).\n2. Do not set autocomplete=\"off\" on those fields.\n\n**Verify:** Open the form in Chrome or Safari with a saved address/profile: each field offers autofill with the right value."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG1.3.5",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "1.3.5"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "required-cue:3.3.2:failure",
              "name": "RequiredFieldHasNoVisibleCue",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Required field has no visible cue"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Required fields shown by colour only (or not at all). Colour-blind and screen-reader users cannot tell which fields are required until they get errors."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/labels-or-instructions.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "Mark required fields in text: \"(required)\" in the label, or an asterisk explained at the top of the form. Add the required attribute (or aria-required=\"true\") so assistive technology announces it. Verify: Grayscale the page (DevTools > Rendering > Emulate vision deficiency: achromatopsia): every required field is still identifiable; screen reader says \"required\".",
                "markdown": "1. Mark required fields in text: \"(required)\" in the label, or an asterisk explained at the top of the form.\n2. Add the required attribute (or aria-required=\"true\") so assistive technology announces it.\n\n**Verify:** Grayscale the page (DevTools > Rendering > Emulate vision deficiency: achromatopsia): every required field is still identifiable; screen reader says \"required\"."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG3.3.2",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "3.3.2"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "mouse-only",
              "name": "ClickHandlerOnAnElementKeyboardUsersCannotReach",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Click handler on an element keyboard users cannot reach"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Controls that only work with a mouse. Keyboard, switch and voice users cannot open the menu, accept the banner or press the button; the journey stops."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/keyboard.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "Use native <button> for actions and <a href> for navigation; avoid clickable <div>/<span>. If a custom control is unavoidable: tabindex=\"0\", role, and Enter/Space handlers. Menus must open on Enter/Space (and click), not only on hover. Verify: Unplug the mouse: complete the journey with Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space, arrows and Esc only.",
                "markdown": "1. Use native <button> for actions and <a href> for navigation; avoid clickable <div>/<span>.\n2. If a custom control is unavoidable: tabindex=\"0\", role, and Enter/Space handlers.\n3. Menus must open on Enter/Space (and click), not only on hover.\n\n**Verify:** Unplug the mouse: complete the journey with Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space, arrows and Esc only."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG2.1.1",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "2.1.1"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "focus-obscured:2.4.7:failure",
              "name": "FocusMovesToAnOffScreenItem",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Focus moves to an off-screen item"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Focused item hidden behind a sticky header, banner or overlay. Keyboard users tab to a link they cannot see, and may activate the wrong thing."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/focus-visible.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "Add scroll-padding-top equal to the sticky header height. Do not let cookie or chat banners cover content while it has focus; make them dismissible. Verify: Tab through the whole page at 390 px and 1440 px: no focused item is entirely covered (2.4.11 AA; partly covered = 2.4.12 AAA).",
                "markdown": "1. Add scroll-padding-top equal to the sticky header height.\n2. Do not let cookie or chat banners cover content while it has focus; make them dismissible.\n\n**Verify:** Tab through the whole page at 390 px and 1440 px: no focused item is entirely covered (2.4.11 AA; partly covered = 2.4.12 AAA)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG2.4.7",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "2.4.7"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "headings-labels:1.3.1:failure",
              "name": "TextStyledAsAHeadingButNotAHeading",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Text styled as a heading but not a heading"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Headings or labels that do not describe their section. Screen-reader users skimming the headings list cannot find the section they need."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/info-and-relationships.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "Turn styled \"fake\" headings into real headings; make heading text describe the section. Remove empty headings; make repeated labels unique (e.g. \"Billing address – City\"). Verify: Headings list reads as a meaningful outline; no empty or duplicate entries.",
                "markdown": "1. Turn styled \"fake\" headings into real headings; make heading text describe the section.\n2. Remove empty headings; make repeated labels unique (e.g. \"Billing address – City\").\n\n**Verify:** Headings list reads as a meaningful outline; no empty or duplicate entries."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG1.3.1",
                  "WCAG2.4.6",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "1.3.1",
                  "2.4.6"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "vague-link",
              "name": "VagueLinkText",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Vague link text"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Vague link text (\"click here\", \"read more\"). Screen-reader users listing links hear several identical \"Read more\" links with no destination."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/link-purpose-in-context.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "Write link text that names the destination (\"Read the lantern care guide\"). If the design needs short text, add visually-hidden context or aria-describedby. Verify: Screen reader links list (NVDA Insert+F7 / VoiceOver rotor): each link makes sense alone.",
                "markdown": "1. Write link text that names the destination (\"Read the lantern care guide\").\n2. If the design needs short text, add visually-hidden context or aria-describedby.\n\n**Verify:** Screen reader links list (NVDA Insert+F7 / VoiceOver rotor): each link makes sense alone."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG2.4.4",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "2.4.4"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "reflow",
              "name": "ContentDoesNotReflowOnSmallScreensOrZoom",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Content does not reflow on small screens or zoom"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Content does not reflow on small screens or zoom. Low-vision users who zoom to 400% (≈320 px wide) must scroll sideways on every line."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/reflow.html",
              "help": {
                "text": "Find the element wider than the viewport (fixed widths, wide tables, long words). Use max-width:100%, flexible grids, overflow-wrap:anywhere; scroll only data tables inside their own container. Verify: Set the browser to 1280 px wide and zoom to 400% (or DevTools 320 px): no horizontal scrollbar for the page.",
                "markdown": "1. Find the element wider than the viewport (fixed widths, wide tables, long words).\n2. Use max-width:100%, flexible grids, overflow-wrap:anywhere; scroll only data tables inside their own container.\n\n**Verify:** Set the browser to 1280 px wide and zoom to 400% (or DevTools 320 px): no horizontal scrollbar for the page."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "WCAG1.4.10",
                  "failure"
                ],
                "kind": "failure",
                "wcag": [
                  "1.4.10"
                ],
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "landmarks:page-has-heading-one:best-practice",
              "name": "PageShouldContainALevelOneHeading",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Page should contain a level-one heading"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Page regions not marked up (no <main>, headings missing). Screen-reader users navigate by landmarks and headings; without them they must listen to the whole page."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://dequeuniversity.com/rules/axe/4.14/page-has-heading-one",
              "help": {
                "text": "Wrap the primary content in one <main>; use <header>, <nav aria-label>, <footer>. Give each page one <h1> and use real <h2>/<h3> headings for sections (not bold text). Verify: Screen reader landmarks list (NVDA D / VoiceOver rotor) shows main and navigation; headings list reads as an outline of the page.",
                "markdown": "1. Wrap the primary content in one <main>; use <header>, <nav aria-label>, <footer>.\n2. Give each page one <h1> and use real <h2>/<h3> headings for sections (not bold text).\n\n**Verify:** Screen reader landmarks list (NVDA D / VoiceOver rotor) shows main and navigation; headings list reads as an outline of the page."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
                  "best-practice"
                ],
                "kind": "best-practice",
                "wcag": [],
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-main",
              "name": "NoMainLandmark",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No main landmark"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Page regions not marked up (no <main>, headings missing). Screen-reader users navigate by landmarks and headings; without them they must listen to the whole page."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://dequeuniversity.com/rules/axe/4.14/landmark-one-main",
              "help": {
                "text": "Wrap the primary content in one <main>; use <header>, <nav aria-label>, <footer>. Give each page one <h1> and use real <h2>/<h3> headings for sections (not bold text). Verify: Screen reader landmarks list (NVDA D / VoiceOver rotor) shows main and navigation; headings list reads as an outline of the page.",
                "markdown": "1. Wrap the primary content in one <main>; use <header>, <nav aria-label>, <footer>.\n2. Give each page one <h1> and use real <h2>/<h3> headings for sections (not bold text).\n\n**Verify:** Screen reader landmarks list (NVDA D / VoiceOver rotor) shows main and navigation; headings list reads as an outline of the page."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "accessibility",
